From 3be805ff443467ed3b559292a39305a34cd86e8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elliotttate <elliotttate@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 18:15:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 123/128] Aurora: pipelines compiled on several threads, and
 the draws skipped while they compile in the log

A draw whose pipeline is still compiling is skipped, and entering a new
place asks for dozens of pipelines at once. One thread compiled them one
after another, so the last were missing from the picture the longest, and
the pipelines the cache loads at start took about 4 s. With Dawn's device
lock on (31401e5f), Dawn's pipeline creation is safe from several threads
(its own asynchronous creation runs on worker threads), so the cache now
starts a quarter of the logical CPUs as compile threads, 1 to 4
(AURORA_PIPELINE_THREADS sets 1-16; without the device lock there is one).
Dolphin compiles shaders on several threads too.

A worker now waits on the queues themselves each time (another may have
taken what it was woken for). The log says, once a second while it
happens, how many draws were skipped and what was compiled for them (new
shaders, or known shaders in a new blend, depth or cull state), and when
the cached pipelines finished compiling.

Measured on the i9 + RTX 5090 (BlueWake, a fresh data folder: the bundled
seed's 213 pipelines and nothing else; two runs each):
- The seed compiled 3.7-4.4 s after start on one thread, 1.06-1.25 s on 4.
- Booting into save states the seed does not cover, draws skipped while
  pipelines compiled, one thread against four: Gohma's room 15,930 and
  20,192 against 3,259 and 3,259; Dragon Roost Cavern's lava room 30,462
  and 32,995 against 2,178 and 2,178; its lava bridge 12,253 and 11,321
  against 1,873 and 1,933. 70 percent of what compiled there was new
  shaders, 30 percent known shaders in a new state.
- Outset route (all pipelines in the seed): no draw skipped either way;
  Smooth Motion dumps identical to the single-thread build's (62 of 62).
